ntdll: the Aurora launcher draws with wined3d in a D3DMetal bottle

On 2026-11-13 Aurora released launcher 1.2.190 (Aurora15Connector.exe), a
Rust rewrite that draws its window with Direct2D (d2d1, dwrite, dxgi). The
.NET 1.2.188 before it drew with GDI. In a game bottle, which CrossOver runs
with CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=d3dmetal because FIFA 15, 17 and 21 need it, the
new launcher shows "Aurora could not open its window" and exits with code 1;
Aurora's updater then logs "The updated Aurora15 launcher exited with code 1
before becoming ready", puts 1.2.188 back, and tries again on the next start.

Under d3dmetal Wine's own d2d1 gets no device:

    warn:d3d10core:D3D10CoreCreateDevice Failed to create device, hr 0x80004005.
    warn:d3d10:d3d10_create_device1 Failed to create a device, hr 0x80004005.
    warn:d2d:d2d_factory_get_device Failed to create device, hr 0x80004005.

The same exe with the bottle switched to wined3d or dxvk: no failure, the
window opens. The backend is bottle-wide (cxbottle.conf), and CrossOver's
per-exe switch lives in its signed compatibility database, so neither can
single out the launcher.

cxcompatdb.so, which start_main_thread loads right after cx_profile_init,
picks the backend for the process from CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND in the unix
environment. So cx_profile_init now sets that variable for this process:
AppDefaults\<exe>\CrossOver-FIFA "GraphicsBackend" (d3dmetal, dxvk,
wined3d; "bottle" for no change), else wined3d for the Aurora launcher: an
exe whose name starts with "aurora15connector" (any case; the updater runs
it under versioned names in launcher-cache), or is "aurora" followed by
something that is no letter or digit -- Aurora.exe, the name it is
downloaded and usually started under. The first two versions of this patch
had only the first rule and left Aurora.exe on D3DMetal, without a window. CX_GAME_PROFILES=0 switches it off with the rest
of the profiles. +cxprofile logs gfx=<backend> when it acted.

The games the launcher starts must keep the bottle's backend, and they would
not on their own: a child starts with its parent's unix environment
(write_env sends environ to CrossOver's loader; the fork path execs with
it), so both CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND and the CX_ACTIVE_GRAPHICS_BACKEND that
cxcompatdb.so derives from it would follow the launcher into FIFA. The
first version of this patch claimed otherwise. So cx_profile_init remembers
the two variables as they were before it and cxcompatdb.so touched them, and
process.c gives every child those values instead (write_env for the loader
path, cx_gfx_child_fixup_environ after fork). Checked with a D3D11 probe in
a d3dmetal bottle: run directly it maps D3DMetal.framework; renamed
aurora15connector-p.exe it maps wined3d; started by a renamed cmd.exe it
maps D3DMetal.framework again.

When testing by hand: an ntdll.so copied into the app needs the lib64 rpath
(install_name_tool -add_rpath @loader_path/../../../lib64) that setup.sh
adds at install. Without it D3DMetal cannot be loaded and every process
falls back to wined3d, whatever this patch does.

Applies on top of game-profiles (it extends cx_profile_init) and after every
other patch that touches dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -2417,6 +2417,53 @@
     }
     buf[n] = 0;
     return n > 0;  /* an empty value says nothing: as if it were not there */
+}
+
+/* The graphics backend for this process alone.  CrossOver picks d3dmetal,
+ * dxvk or wined3d per process: cxcompatdb.so, which start_main_thread loads
+ * right after cx_profile_init, reads CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND from the unix
+ * environment.  A game bottle says d3dmetal for the games, but under d3dmetal
+ * Wine's own d2d1 gets no device (D3D10CoreCreateDevice fails with E_FAIL),
+ * so a launcher that draws with Direct2D -- Aurora15Connector 1.2.190 on --
+ * cannot open its window.  The variable is set here for this process; a
+ * child would inherit it with the rest of the unix environment, so children
+ * are started with the bottle's values again (cx_gfx_child_* below) and the
+ * games a launcher starts keep the bottle's backend.
+ *
+ * First of: HKCU\...\AppDefaults\<exe>\CrossOver-FIFA "GraphicsBackend"
+ * (d3dmetal, dxvk, wined3d, or "bottle" for no change), then the built-in
+ * rule (an exe named "aurora.exe" or starting "aurora15connector" gets
+ * wined3d).  NULL: keep the bottle's. */
+/* While this process runs with its own backend, the bottle's values of the two
+ * variables that pick one, as they were before cxcompatdb.so ran: what every
+ * child must get instead of this process's (cx_gfx_child_*). */
+static BOOL cx_gfx_changed;
+static struct { const char *name; char *bottle; } cx_gfx_vars[] =
+{
+    { "CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND" },
+    { "CX_ACTIVE_GRAPHICS_BACKEND" },  /* set by cxcompatdb.so for itself */
+};
+
+static const char *cx_graphics_backend( const WCHAR *exe, HANDLE key, char *buf, size_t size )
+{
+#define CX_ALNUM(c) ((((c) | 0x20) >= 'a' && ((c) | 0x20) <= 'z') || ((c) >= '0' && (c) <= '9'))
+    static const char aurora[] = "aurora15connector";
+    unsigned int i;
+
+    if (cx_reg_string( key, "GraphicsBackend", buf, size ))
+    {
+        if (!strcasecmp( buf, "bottle" )) return NULL;
+        if (!strcasecmp( buf, "d3dmetal" ) || !strcasecmp( buf, "dxvk" ) || !strcasecmp( buf, "wined3d" ))
+            return buf;
+        WARN_(cxprofile)( "unknown GraphicsBackend %s for %s, ignored\n", debugstr_a(buf), debugstr_w(exe) );
+    }
+    /* "aurora15connector*", or "aurora" and then no letter or digit: Aurora.exe,
+     * the name the launcher is downloaded under ("aurora (1).exe" too).  Not
+     * aurora15client, aurora17connector, aurora21-mathbridge. */
+    for (i = 0; aurora[i]; i++)
+        if (!exe[i] || (exe[i] | 0x20) != aurora[i])
+            return i >= 6 && exe[6] && !CX_ALNUM( exe[6] ) ? "wined3d" : NULL;
+    return "wined3d";
 }
 
